    {"id":"DUR04-FPC-STAGING-HEAP-BYTES","owner_contract":"DUR-04 / FIRST_PRODUCTION_CONTENT_PROFILE/v1","resource":"decoded untrusted-content heap charged to one staged pair excluding separately bounded immutable raw artifacts","unit":"bytes","hard_maximum":32768,"configurable_range":{"minimum":32768,"maximum":32768},"failure_category":"CAPACITY_EXCEEDED","allocation_impact":"A bounded staging allocator refuses the allocation and leaves active state unchanged.","client_visible":false,"boundary_tests":["charged usage through 32768 bytes succeeds when semantic limits pass","the next charged byte rejects staging","allocator exhaustion leaves prior active generation unchanged"],"notes":"Raw artifact bytes are separately bounded at 15430 and are not charged here. Worst-case decoded semantic field payload is 14720 bytes: server 88 fields * 128 = 11264; client 27 fields * 128 = 3456. Required compact representation additionally budgets at most 920 bytes for 115 8-byte string descriptors, 224 for 28 8-byte record descriptors, 168 for 21 8-byte definition-index entries, 192 for 24 8-byte reference entries, 2048 for artifact/section/revision descriptors and 8192 for validation scratch: total at most 26464, leaving 6304 bytes below the 32768 hard cap. Any implementation representation that cannot fit must fail this profile rather than raise the limit."},
